<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <%- include('../../partials/head') %>
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('../../partials/helpers') %>
  <header><%- include('../../partials/navbar') %></header>

  <main class="container py-5">
    <% if (locals.flash) { %>
      <div class="alert alert-<%= flash.type === 'error' ? 'danger' : 'success' %> alert-dismissible fade show border-0 shadow-sm mb-4" role="alert">
        <i class="bi bi-<%= flash.type === 'error' ? 'exclamation-triangle' : 'check-circle' %> me-2"></i><%= flash.message %>
        <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="alert"></button>
      </div>
    <% } %>

    <div class="mb-4">
      <p class="text-muted small mb-1"><a href="/aisworg/seu/identity">&larr; Identity Management</a></p>
      <h2 class="h3 mb-1 text-dark fw-bold"><i class="bi bi-patch-check me-2"></i>Badge Management</h2>
      <p class="text-muted small mb-0">
        Badge model (Phase 10, extended by CR-006) — an identity holds a <em>set</em> of badges: Layer 1 Platform
        (unscoped), Layer 2a Tenant Admin (scoped to one Tenant), and noun &times; verb authoring badges
        (<code>{noun}_{verb}</code>, e.g. <code>pack_define</code>) — not one flat role. The earlier Layer 2b
        Creator/Reviewer/Approver family is retired (nothing has enforced it since noun &times; verb shipped) and no
        longer appears here.
      </p>
    </div>

    <%
      // Bug fix: "badge grants pagination is taking me back to the badge
      // catalog as the active tab" — Bootstrap's tab state is client-side
      // only, so a full-page reload (every pagination/sort/search link on the
      // Grants tab is a plain GET) always re-opened Badge Catalog by default.
      // The route computes which tab this request is actually "on" from the
      // query string; render that one active instead of always Catalog.
      const onGrantsTab = locals.activeTab === 'grants';
    %>
    <ul class="nav nav-tabs mb-4" id="badgeTabs" role="tablist">
      <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
        <button class="nav-link <%= onGrantsTab ? '' : 'active' %>" id="catalog-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-bs-target="#catalog-pane" type="button" role="tab">
          <i class="bi bi-collection me-1"></i>Badge Catalog
        </button>
      </li>
      <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
        <button class="nav-link <%= onGrantsTab ? 'active' : '' %>" id="grants-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-bs-target="#grants-pane" type="button" role="tab">
          <i class="bi bi-patch-check me-1"></i>Badge Grants
        </button>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="tab-content" id="badgeTabsContent">

      <!-- ═══ Badge Catalog ═══ -->
      <div class="tab-pane fade <%= onGrantsTab ? '' : 'show active' %>" id="catalog-pane" role="tabpanel">
        <%
          const platformBadges = badgeTypes.filter(function(b) { return b.scope_kind === 'None'; });
          const tenantBadges   = badgeTypes.filter(function(b) { return b.scope_kind === 'Tenant'; });
          function tenantCode(id) { const t = tenants.find(function(t){ return t.id === id; }); return t ? t.code : id; }
        %>
        <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-4">
          <div class="card-body">
            <h6 class="text-uppercase text-muted small fw-bold mb-2"><i class="bi bi-hdd-stack me-1"></i>Platform (Layer 1) — unscoped</h6>
            <table class="table table-sm align-middle mb-4">
              <thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Name</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <% platformBadges.forEach(function(b) { %>
                  <tr><td><code><%= b.code %></code></td><td><%= b.name %></td></tr>
                <% }) %>
              </tbody>
            </table>

            <h6 class="text-uppercase text-muted small fw-bold mb-2"><i class="bi bi-building me-1"></i>Tenant (Layer 2a) — scoped to one Tenant</h6>
            <table class="table table-sm align-middle mb-4">
              <thead><tr><th>Tenant</th><th>Code</th><th>Name</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <% tenantBadges.forEach(function(b) { %>
                  <tr><td class="small"><%= b.tenant_id ? tenantCode(b.tenant_id) : '— Platform-recommended —' %></td><td><code><%= b.code %></code></td><td><%= b.name %></td></tr>
                <% }) %>
              </tbody>
            </table>

            <h6 class="text-uppercase text-muted small fw-bold mb-2"><i class="bi bi-diagram-3 me-1"></i>Authoring (noun &times; verb) — Pack / Template / Profile / Objective / Transition Definition</h6>
            <p class="text-muted small mb-2">
              <code>{noun}_{verb}</code> badges (e.g. <code>pack_define</code>, <code>objective_propose</code>) —
              CR-006's replacement for the old SEU-scoped Creator/Reviewer/Approver family, which is retired (nothing
              has enforced it since). These aren't catalog rows here — the vocabulary that defines which nouns/verbs
              exist and which pairs are valid is managed on its own pages:
              <a href="/aisworg/seu/authority/nouns">Work outcome (Nouns)</a>,
              <a href="/aisworg/seu/authority/verbs">Work process (Verbs)</a>,
              <a href="/aisworg/seu/authority/mapping">Mapping</a>. Actual grants of them show up in the
              <strong>Badge Grants</strong> tab below like any other badge.
            </p>

            <p class="text-muted small mb-2">Rename an inherited badge (same code, new name for one Tenant), or add a new one derived from a Platform-recommended badge (§8.1) — it inherits that parent's scope kind. Layer 1 (Platform) badges are excluded from Tenant customization.</p>
            <form method="POST" action="/aisworg/seu/identity/badge-types" class="row g-2 align-items-end">
              <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
              <div class="col-auto">
                <label class="form-label small mb-1">Tenant</label>
                <select name="tenantId" class="form-select form-select-sm" required>
                  <% tenants.forEach(function(t) { %><option value="<%= t.id %>"><%= t.code %></option><% }) %>
                </select>
              </div>
              <div class="col-auto"><label class="form-label small mb-1">Code</label><input name="code" class="form-control form-control-sm" placeholder="senior_tenant_admin" required></div>
              <div class="col-auto"><label class="form-label small mb-1">Name</label><input name="name" class="form-control form-control-sm" placeholder="Senior Tenant Admin" required></div>
              <input type="hidden" name="scopeKind" value="Tenant">
              <div class="col-auto"><label class="form-label small mb-1">derived_from (parent's code)</label><input name="derivedFrom" class="form-control form-control-sm" placeholder="tenant_admin" required></div>
              <div class="col-auto"><button type="submit" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary">Save badge</button></div>
            </form>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ═══ Badge Grants ═══ -->
      <div class="tab-pane fade <%= onGrantsTab ? 'show active' : '' %>" id="grants-pane" role="tabpanel">
        <% const _base = locals.listBasePath || '/aisworg/seu/identity/badges'; %>
        <%- include('../../partials/listControls', { list: list, listBasePath: _base, searchPlaceholder: 'Search holder / badge' }) %>
        <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-4">
          <div class="card-body">
            <table class="table table-sm align-middle">
              <thead><tr>
                <th><%- sortLink('Holder', 'holder', list, _base) %></th>
                <th><%- sortLink('Badge', 'badge', list, _base) %></th>
                <th>Scope</th><th>Status</th><th></th>
              </tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <% if (list.total === 0) { %>
                  <tr><td colspan="5" class="text-muted small text-center py-3"><%= list.q ? 'No grants match your search.' : 'No grants.' %></td></tr>
                <% } %>
                <% list.items.forEach(function(g) { %>
                  <tr>
                    <td class="small"><%= g.holderEmail || g.holder_id %></td>
                    <td><code><%= g.badge_type %></code></td>
                    <td class="small text-muted"><%= g.scope_id || '' %></td>
                    <td><span class="state-badge state-<%= g.status %>"><%= g.status %></span></td>
                    <td>
                      <% if (g.status === 'Active') { %>
                        <form method="POST" action="/aisworg/seu/identity/grants/<%= g.id %>/revoke">
                          <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
                          <button type="submit" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-danger">Revoke</button>
                        </form>
                      <% } %>
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                <% }) %>
              </tbody>
            </table>
            <p class="text-muted small mb-2">Every grant is one row — an identity accumulates as many as it holds (§9). Scope only applies to Tenant-scoped badges (e.g. tenant_admin — scope id is the Tenant id); noun &times; verb authoring badges and Layer 1 Platform badges leave it blank.</p>
            <form method="POST" action="/aisworg/seu/identity/grants" class="row g-2 align-items-end">
              <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
              <div class="col-auto"><label class="form-label small mb-1">Holder email</label><input name="holderEmail" type="email" class="form-control form-control-sm" required></div>
              <div class="col-auto"><label class="form-label small mb-1">Badge code</label><input name="badgeType" class="form-control form-control-sm" placeholder="pack_define" required></div>
              <div class="col-auto"><label class="form-label small mb-1">Scope id (tenant id, when the badge is Tenant-scoped)</label><input name="scopeId" class="form-control form-control-sm"></div>
              <div class="col-auto"><button type="submit" class="btn btn-sm btn-primary">Grant badge</button></div>
            </form>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </main>

  <%- include('../../partials/footer') %>
</body>
</html>
